From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 07:45:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] drm/bridge: dw-hdmi: Send HDR10+ at a mode with no HDMI VIC

hdmi_config_hdr10plus_infoframe() asks for the mode's HDMI VSIF only to
learn whether a 3D VSIF needs the slot and whether an HDMI_VIC moves the
VIC to the AVI InfoFrame, but returned when the helper fails. It fails
for every mode with neither an HDMI_VIC nor 3D, 1080p and most 4K modes
among them, so the HDR10+ VSIF was never sent there.

Take a failure as no HDMI VSIF of its own: send the HDR10+ one, and leave
the AVI VIC as hdmi_config_AVI() set it.

Signed-off-by: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-hdmi.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-hdmi.c
@@ -2008,10 +2008,12 @@
 					    const struct drm_display_mode *mode)
 {
 	struct hdmi_vendor_infoframe frame;
+	bool hdmi_vsif;
 	int i;
 
-	if (drm_hdmi_vendor_infoframe_from_display_mode(&frame, connector, mode) ||
-	    frame.s3d_struct != HDMI_3D_STRUCTURE_INVALID)
+	/* fails for a mode with neither an HDMI_VIC nor 3D: no HDMI VSIF of its own, the usual case */
+	hdmi_vsif = !drm_hdmi_vendor_infoframe_from_display_mode(&frame, connector, mode);
+	if (hdmi_vsif && frame.s3d_struct != HDMI_3D_STRUCTURE_INVALID)
 		return;
 
 	hdmi_mask_writeb(hdmi, 0, HDMI_FC_DATAUTO0, HDMI_FC_DATAUTO0_VSD_OFFSET,
@@ -2028,7 +2030,7 @@
 			 HDMI_FC_DATAUTO0_VSD_MASK);
 
 	/* Without HDMI_VIC in the VSIF, the AVI InfoFrame names the CTA VIC. */
-	if (frame.vic)
+	if (hdmi_vsif && frame.vic)
 		hdmi_writeb(hdmi, drm_match_cea_mode(mode), HDMI_FC_AVIVID);
 }
 
